cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this software using these metadata.
type: software
title: "Silver-rate lower bound for gradient descent, strongly convex case: Lean formalization"
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: https://github.com/Jeong2357/silver-rate-strongly-convex-lean
license: GPL-3.0-only
authors:
  - family-names: Jeong
    given-names: Yechan
    affiliation: Department of Mathematical Sciences, Seoul National University
    email: yechan@snu.ac.kr
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-1476-0666
  - family-names: Hong
    given-names: Youngjoon
    affiliation: Department of Mathematical Sciences, Seoul National University
    email: hongyj@snu.ac.kr
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4956-8660
abstract: >-
  A Lean formalization of the sharp silver-rate lower bound for gradient
  descent on smooth strongly convex functions with arbitrary predetermined
  real stepsizes. The theorem gives a uniform exp(-C n kappa^(-nu)) lower
  bound for both worst-case relative squared-distance and function-value
  errors, where nu = 1/log_2(1 + sqrt(2)), for all sufficiently large
  condition numbers and all horizons in positive finite Euclidean dimensions.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - gradient descent
  - strongly convex optimization
  - stepsize schedules
  - lower bounds
